    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 25 tests pass, including the two new `Cp15Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the Owner resource so it returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern used for the derived `membershipNumber` field:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec at build time, giving it the getter/setter).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` that populates `membershipTier` via a new `membershipTier(owner)` helper:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n       boolean noNamesakes = owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0;\n       boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty();\n       return (noNamesakes && hasEmail) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe null-safe checks mirror the surrounding mapper code so owners without a namesake count or email serialize as `BRONZE` cleanly.",
